  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 5.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to design and deliver innovative, flexible and inclusive learning options, encompassing work-based learning and quality apprenticeships</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Labour and Partnership Relations  and the National Training Institute jointly implemented an online employability training programme to mitigate the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic. The training focused in the areas of Core/Soft Skills, Occupational Safety and Health (OSH), and Entrepreneurial Skills. The programme  served to promote an employment-centred recovery which achieved the following objectives:

(a) Enhanced the employability of 912 workers receiving income support from public       interventions as a consequence of the reduction of the economic activity due to measures implemented to limit the spread of COVID-19;

(b) Supported an employment-centred recovery after COVID-19 in which affected workers resume work quickly and increase their capacities to perform duties more efficiently, or to engage in self-employment; and
(c) Delivered a flexible online and inclusive skills programme targeting women, youth and persons in vulnerable situations. 

The training programme achieved a satisfactory participation rate: 
- One thousand and seventy-eight (1078) persons registered for the courses, and nine hundred and twelve (912) persons met the eligibility requirements and were enrolled in the courses.
- One hundred and ninety-seven (197) persons completed the Core Skills course.
- One hundred and fifty-one (151) persons completed the Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) course.
- One hundred and twenty-one (121) persons completed the Entrepreneurship course.

Evaluation of the training programme indicated overall satisfaction with the e-learning experience, and provided positive feedback on the quality of the course. The ILO provided support in the design of the course materials, delivery and coordination of the training programme.</narrative>
   </description>
